      "rationale": "Implementation element FB2-SW-IMP-000001 is the code location in which the reference project's FB2-SW-DSN-000001 acquisition, PEC-validation and publication responsibilities are carried: the pinned source's LTC_Trigger sequencer, its LTC_StartVoltageMeasurement command selection, its LTC_CheckPec per-LTC integrity gate, its LTC_SaveRxToVoltageBuffer reassembly and the DMA-backed SPI transfer the design selects, which the source realises through SPI_TransmitReceiveDataDma and AFE_DmaCallback rather than through the symbols the design names. The link runs from the implementation to the design because that is the direction master prompt section 13 declares for implements (implementation element -> design/requirement).",
      "provenance": "derived",
      "review_state": "reviewed",
      "change_suspect_status": false,
      "reorientation_note": "RE-ORIENTED 2026-10-02. This link previously read FB2-SW-DSN-000001 --implements--> FB2-SW-SWR-000001 (design on the source side, requirement on the target side) with the rationale 'Design implements software requirement'. That direction is the inverse of the one master prompt section 13 declares for implements, and the old rationale asserted the relationship rather than describing it. The link_id is unchanged so the record's identity stays traceable. The requirement-level relationship the old link stood for is now carried by FB2-LNK-IMP-000104 (FB2-SW-IMP-000001 --implements--> FB2-SW-SWR-000001) and the requirement-to-design allocation by FB2-LNK-ALW-000101 (FB2-SW-SWR-000001 --allocated_to--> FB2-SW-DSN-000001)."
    },
